{"schema":1,"function":"gammainc_large","description":"Regularized lower incomplete gamma function P(a, x) for large shapes a >= 1e8","inputs":["a","x"],"outputs":["y"],"points":51,"tolerance":{"rel":1e-12,"reason":"The function and method of gammainc and gamma_cdf, with their tolerance. The condition number |x f(x) / P| grows like k sqrt(a) at x = a + k sqrt(a) (9.5e5 at a = 1e9, k = -30), so a method that rounds x / a would lose about 1e-10; one that forms x - a exactly (Sterbenz's lemma) and expands in (x - a) / a (Temme, DLMF 8.12; Boost) loses about k^2 2^-53 (1e-13 at k = 30). Far from the bulk P rounds to 0 or 1. SciPy's worst error is 2.7e-15 except in the lower tail at x = a - 10 sqrt(a) and a - 30 sqrt(a): 13% and 0.24% off at a = 1e8, 53% and 15% off at a = 1e9 (P about 7e-24 and 2e-198; numerical integration confirms mpmath)"},"grid":"a in {1e8, 1e9, 1e10, 1e15, 1e20} x x in {1e8, 2e8, a/2, 0.9a, 1.1a, 2a, 1e300}, plus x = a + k sqrt(a) for a in {1e8, 1e9} and k in {-30, -10, -3, -1, 0, 1, 3, 10, 30}","mpmath":{"version":"1.4.1","dps":[50,100]},"scipy":{"version":"1.18.1","function":"scipy.special.gammainc"},"numpy":"2.5.4","python":"3.13"}
